      "widgets_values": [
        "## Writing the video description\n\nH3 reads one prose block, not a tag list. What reliably works, in this order:\n\n1. **Look + subject continuity** - one sentence: \"photoreal, same face/hair/outfit as the starting\n   image, shallow depth of field with the background far out of focus\". Repeating the identity and\n   the blurred background here is what keeps them from drifting mid-clip.\n2. **A timestamped beat list** - `[0.0s-1.2s] ...`, `[1.2s-2.8s] ...`. Say what the *body* does\n   (blink, breathe, turn, tuck hair, smile) and what the *camera* does (hold, drift in, gentle\n   handheld). Small human motions read far better than big ones at 5 s.\n3. **Dialogue in quotes** - \"She says: \\\"...\\\"\". H3 lip-syncs it and speaks it. Keep it to one or\n   two short lines for a 5 s clip; anything longer gets rushed.\n4. **An `Audio:` line** - voice character, then background. If you do *not* want music, say\n   \"no music\" - silence is not the default.\n5. **A negative tail** - \"no cuts, no scene changes, no text overlays, no extra fingers\".\n\nRules of thumb: one continuous shot per 5 s clip; describe motion, never a still pose; do not\nre-describe the scenery the starting image already shows (the model can see it) - spend the words\non movement, speech, and what must *not* change."
      ],
      "title": "How to write the description"
    },
